Z||000003||87FieroGTx||11-02-2001||04:37 PM|||| Sounds like my race with the infamous PINK MR2 Only he left me from the line and never stopped.<P> Who would have thought a Pink car would have 525rwhp! <P> The (GUY) said he has over 25k into the "PINK ROCKET"<P> That car reminds me of a southpark episode!<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75+ shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.9 13.5 1/4||||reg||1
Z||000004||NOS3800||11-02-2001||05:55 PM||||My brother(Lildv1L) and I went to a Import Shootout here in Southern MD a month ago. There was a white 240SX on a trailer with slicks in line behind us. We got there before the gates opened so we walked around it a bit, kinda snickering. I mean who ever thought a 240 can be fast? We thought if anything, it had a Chevy V8. There was also a 4 door Jetta behind the 240, also on a trailer. It had stickers ALL over it, proclaiming it to be the "Fastest 4-door VW in the World".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>Anyway, we were SHOCKEd when the damn 240 ran a low 12 second pass! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Turns out it had a twin turbo setup, out of a SILVIA. I am guessing it is what 1FST2M6 explained. "But" it was trailered, like that makes the hurt better. BUt the jetta, get this, ran low 15's! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Come on, there has to be faster Jettas out there!<BR>But at least you gave him a scare, you DID give him a scare, didn't you?<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||11
Z||000005||Formula88||11-02-2001||06:42 PM||||Cool!  Rule No. 1 about racing: No matter how fast you are, someone's always faster.  Still, it is nice he was cool.  I typically find the people with the seriously fast cars are cooler than the wannabes.  They don't have a chip on their shoulder or anything to prove.  They KNOW they've got a fast car.  I always felt, hey, if you're faster than me, I wanna see it!  Like the time I ran up against a 427 6-pack Corvette!  I was in a 71 Mercury Police package (429, basically a slightly detuned 429SCJ) and he walked away from me like the Millenniuum Falcon hitting Hyperdrive.  But it was a pleasure to watch.  I met up with him later, and he was cool.  I even thanked him for the experience.||||reg||1
